{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/811262-feeding-and-specific-preferences","id":811262,"title":"Feeding and 'Specific Preferences'","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-18T12:36:52-08:00","id":811262,"title":"Feeding and 'Specific Preferences'","content":"On the Feeding Modifier chart (p.108) the phrase &quot;specific preferences&quot; shows up. What exactly does that mean? Is it some specific preference among the Hungers in general, or does it mean within a given Hunger?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-18T12:48:43-08:00","id":811268,"title":"","content":"See the example with Mrs. Winters on page 110.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-18T18:35:23-08:00","id":811438,"title":"","content":"It's like, if you have a Hunger for Ruin, you can feed on destroying anything that's important to someone... but if your Horror has a specific &quot;taste&quot; for, say, smashing up fancy cars, then taking a sledgehammer to a a deluxe Porsche will be more satisfying (give you more feeding dice) than slashing the tires on a junker or burning down someone's house.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1419-wardragon","name":"WarDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1419_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1052"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T09:54:52-08:00","id":811890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WarDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/811262-feeding-and-specific-preferences?p=811438#post811438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's like, if you have a Hunger for Ruin, you can feed on destroying anything that's important to someone... but if your Horror has a specific &quot;taste&quot; for, say, smashing up fancy cars, then taking a sledgehammer to a a deluxe Porsche will be more satisfying (give you more feeding dice) than slashing the tires on a junker or burning down someone's house.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or breaking up a marriage, or crashing someone's stock portfolio and thus sending them to the poor house.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T09:58:59-08:00","id":811893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HaplessWithDice</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/811262-feeding-and-specific-preferences?p=811890#post811890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or breaking up a marriage, or crashing someone's stock portfolio and thus sending them to the poor house.</div> </div> </div> </div>Marriage and the economy are kind of above the pay grade of the Ravagers as primeval disaster-beasts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T10:04:59-08:00","id":811903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/811262-feeding-and-specific-preferences?p=811893#post811893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Marriage and the economy are kind of above the pay grade of the Ravagers as primeval disaster-beasts.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't be so sure. What is a Marriage but a formal bond contract between two humans? Mated pairs exist in very primordial society so a ravager feeding off breaking up couples is not outside of their domain.<br /> <br /> After 1929 I'm sure there are Ravagers who feed like kings from ruining people's lives and livelihood by analiating their fiances making their children go from wearing the best clothes to wearing 2nd hand clothes from a Goodwill. There are a lot of ways to ruin simply trashing physical things is one way to do it beasts are as much a metaphor as anything else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T10:10:27-08:00","id":811908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HaplessWithDice</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/811262-feeding-and-specific-preferences?p=811903#post811903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are a lot of ways to ruin simply trashing physical things is one way to do it beasts are as much a metaphor as anything else.</div> </div> </div> </div>Literally none of the many examples are flush with this. You'd have more luck with a Nemesis or a Predator on that front.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T10:50:54-08:00","id":811940,"title":"","content":"Beasts are the metaphor, the moral at the end of the story, though they might not consider themselves such. The wolf in Little Red Riding Hood is a perfect example, in the original French Text did you know there was no huntsman, of course in the original french version the wolf's teeth were never mentioned but rather his legs and the story was a warning against sexual predators? Such a being would also be a Ravager as he would be destroying or ruining innocence.<br /> <br /> Depending on Culture destroying a marriage would fit the exact definition for High Satiety.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beast the Primordial Page 110</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> High Satiety: For high Satiety, the destruction must be<br /> <i>obvious and extensive</i>, or the<i>target must be widely accepted to<br /> be valuable</i> or in use by many people.</div> </div> </div> </div>Breaking up a couple who are engaged but not married wold fit under moderate because while engament is valued it isn't valued as much as a actual marriage which people will go to even the cost of their lives (or someone elses) to save. Again Italics added for emphasis.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beast the Primordial Page 110</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Moderate Satiety: The item destroyed must be <i>extremely<br /> important to at least a small group of people</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>While the examples are of more direct ruination, don't forget that less direct examples can exist. Everyone would agree that if a Wealthy man lost his wealth it could feed a Myrid of hungers depending on how he lost it. Let us say a Ravager Stockbroker built up his account then in one action one bit a bad advice brought the man down to pennyless. Is this man not Ruined? Going from eating Fine Organic Steak USDA Prime, to eating beans and rice because he cannot afford meat? Even McDonalds is outside of his price range. How can we not call is Ruined? Would I call it high satiety? Not really probably better fitting on low. His family is crying, they will be focused on the loss rather than the destructor, everything is there ready to be called a Low ruin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T11:16:43-08:00","id":811958,"title":"","content":"It's not the what, but the why that matters. There's a lot of overlap in what one can do to feed, but the logic behind the act has to line up with the Hunger.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}